cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Urban-Future-Weather Engine or its EPW corpus in your
  research, please cite it.
title: >-
  NEPENTHE | Urban-Future-Weather Engine: a map-first explorer for
  city-scale, multi-era future weather files
authors:
  - family-names: Karimi
    given-names: Alireza
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6296-9496
    affiliation: Universidad de Sevilla
type: software
version: 1.3.1
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Alirezza18/urban-future-weather-engine
abstract: >-
  A web platform that serves future microclimate weather files (EPW) for
  building- and district-scale climate-resilience simulation. The engine
  fuses EURO-CORDEX regional climate projections, heatwave-preserving
  morphing and Urban Heat Island intensification (Urban Weather Generator
  on a 50 x 50 m grid driven by 3D GIS morphology) into hourly weather
  files for historical, mid-century and 2084 horizons, and exposes them
  through an interactive map with direct downloads and per-file provenance.
keywords:
  - EPW
  - future weather files
  - urban heat island
  - climate change
  - building performance simulation
  - morphing
  - EURO-CORDEX
  - urban climate
